_X$-module.\n\\begin{enumerate}\n\\item If the support of $\\mathcal{F}$ is proper over $S$, then\n$\\mathcal{F}$ is universally pure relative to $S$.\n\\item If $f$ is proper, then\n$\\mathcal{F}$ is universally pure relative to $S$.\n\\item If $f$ is proper, then $X$ is universally pure relative to $S$.\n\\end{enumerate}", "pass3_eligible": false, "published": false, "schema": "maththm.four-complete-chapters.standalone-editorial-draft.v1", "section_ambient_hypotheses_auto_inherited": [], "section_end_line": 5164, "section_index": 178, "section_key": "s178", "section_start_line": 5009, "section_title": "Examples of relatively pure sheaves", "source_enumerated_clauses": ["If the support of $\\mathcal{F}$ is proper over $S$, then\n$\\mathcal{F}$ is universally pure relative to $S$.", "If $f$ is proper, then\n$\\mathcal{F}$ is universally pure relative to $S$.", "If $f$ is proper, then $X$ is universally pure relative to $S$."], "source_filename": "flat.tex", "source_formal_environment": "lemma", "source_formal_environment_end_line": 5026, "source_formal_environment_start_line": 5015, "source_inline_reference_labels": [], "source_label": "lemma-proper-pure", "source_logical_form": "listed_assertions_with_individual_guards", "source_named_reference_labels": [], "source_proof_screened": false, "source_revision": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_scoped_conventions_and_situations": [], "source_statement_line": 5015, "source_url": "https://github.com/stacks/stacks-project/blob/a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14/flat.tex#L5015", "standalone_statement_tex": "Let $f : X \\to S$ be a morphism of schemes which is of finite type.\nLet $\\mathcal{F}$ be a finite type quasi-coherent $\\mathcal{O}_X$-module.\n\\begin{enumerate}\n\\item If the support of $\\mathcal{F}$ is proper over $S$, then\n$\\mathcal{F}$ is universally pure relative to $S$.\n\\item If $f$ is proper, then\n$\\mathcal{F}$ is universally pure relative to $S$.\n\\item If $f$ is proper, then $X$ is universally pure relative to $S$.\n\\end{enumerate}"}
